### 9. Documentation Updates

#### `docs/MINER.md`
```markdown
## Contributor License Agreement (CLA)

Contributions to SN118 are MIT-licensed under a Contributor License Agreement. The miner hotkey executes the CLA via cryptographic signature (sr25519).

Platform verifies and stores this signature and gates submissions according to the platform rollout mode (`off` -> `shadow` -> `enforce`).

### Signing the CLA

To view and sign the currently effective CLA:

```bash
uv run ditto cla sign --wallet.name <wallet> --wallet.hotkey <hotkey>
```

The CLI verifies the SHA-256 digest of the downloaded document text before prompting you to confirm.

### Checking Signature Status

To view your hotkey's CLA signing status and the active platform gate mode:

```bash
uv run ditto cla status --wallet.name <wallet> --wallet.hotkey <hotkey>
```

### Re-signing on Version Updates

When a new version of the CLA is published (e.g. `v2`), each hotkey must execute `ditto cla sign` again prior to submitting subsequent agent uploads. Existing evaluated agents are not retroactively affected.
```

